      "summaries": {
        "en": "nn-zero-to-hero is a hands-on course by Andrej Karpathy that teaches neural networks from scratch using Python and Jupyter notebooks. It demystifies deep learning by building backpropagation, neural networks, and transformers step by step, emphasizing mathematical intuition and code implementation. Ideal for learners who want to truly understand how models work under the hood, the course provides practical exercises to build and train your own networks, making advanced concepts accessible.",
        "zh": "nn-zero-to-hero 是 Andrej Karpathy 推出的神经网络实战课程，以 Jupyter Notebook 为载体，通过 Python 代码逐步实现反向传播、神经网络和 Transformer 等核心概念。课程强调数学直觉与代码实现紧密结合，帮助学习者深入理解模型底层原理。内容从线性模型到完整语言模型循序渐进，每环节配有可运行代码示例，适合希望扎实掌握深度学习基础的研究者或工程师。",
        "es": "nn-zero-to-hero is a hands-on course by Andrej Karpathy that teaches neural networks from scratch using Python and Jupyter notebooks. It demystifies deep learning by building backpropagation, neural networks, and transformers step by step, emphasizing mathematical intuition and code implementation. Ideal for learners who want to truly understand how models work under the hood, the course provides practical exercises to build and train your own networks, making advanced concepts accessible.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "nn-zero-to-hero gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "nn-zero-to-hero is a hands-on course by Andrej Karpathy that teaches neural networks from scratch using Python and Jupyter notebooks. It demystifies deep learning by building backpropagation, neural networks, and transformers step by step, emphasizing mathematical intuition and code implementation. Ideal for learners who want to truly understand how models work under the hood, the course provides practical exercises to build and train your own networks, making advanced concepts accessible.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/karpathy/nn-zero-to-hero for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
